<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<section xml:id="num-standard-form">
  <title>Standard Form</title>

  <objectives>
    <title>Learning Outcomes</title>
    <ul>
      <li><xref ref="lo-n-15" /> — Express numbers in standard form</li>
      <li><xref ref="lo-n-16" /> — Calculations in standard form</li>
    </ul>
  </objectives>

  <p>
    <term>Standard form</term> (scientific notation) writes a number as <m>a \times 10^n</m>
    where <m>1 \leq a \lt 10</m> and <m>n</m> is an integer.
  </p>
  <p>
    Large numbers: <m>340\,000 = 3.4 \times 10^5</m>.
    Small numbers: <m>0.000045 = 4.5 \times 10^{-5}</m>.
  </p>
  <p>
    To multiply in standard form: <m>(3 \times 10^4) \times (2 \times 10^3) = 6 \times 10^7</m>.
    To divide: <m>(6 \times 10^8) \div (3 \times 10^5) = 2 \times 10^3</m>.
  </p>

  <exercises xml:id="exs-standard-form">
    <title>Exercises</title>

    <exercise xml:id="ex-to-standard">
      <statement><p>Write <m>0.000072</m> in standard form.</p></statement>
      <answer><p><m>7.2 \times 10^{-5}</m></p></answer>
    </exercise>

    <exercise xml:id="ex-standard-multiply">
      <statement><p>Calculate: <m>(4 \times 10^3) \times (5 \times 10^4)</m>. Give your answer in standard form.</p></statement>
      <answer><p><m>2 \times 10^8</m></p></answer>
      <solution><p><m>4 \times 5 = 20</m> and <m>10^3 \times 10^4 = 10^7</m>, so <m>20 \times 10^7 = 2 \times 10^8</m>.</p></solution>
    </exercise>

  </exercises>

</section>
